        "file": "app/assets/stylesheets/common/foundation/mixins.scss",
        "title": "align-items mixin emits invalid or incorrect legacy declarations",
        "description": "`-ms-align-items` is not a real property, so it is dead output. The legacy `-webkit-box-align` and `-ms-flex-align` properties use different keywords from the standard ones: `start`, `end`, `center`, `baseline` and `stretch`, not `flex-start` or `flex-end`. Passing a standard value like flex-start or flex-end would produce invalid declarations for those engines. Current callers pass only center and baseline, which work. The mixin also has inconsistent indentation and trailing whitespace.",
        "severity": "low",
        "confidence": 30,
        "anchor": "@mixin align-items($alignment) {\n    -webkit-box-align: $alignment;\n    -webkit-align-items: $alignment;\n    -ms-flex-align: $alignment;  \n    -ms-align-items: $alignment;",
        "evidence": "The mixin copies a single $alignment value into -webkit-box-align, -ms-flex-align and the invented -ms-align-items. The legacy property keyword sets differ from the standard align-items set.",
