        "title": "Flexbox applied to a clearfix container makes the clearfix pseudo-elements flex items",
        "description": "The header template gives `.contents` the `clearfix` class, whose :before/:after pseudo-elements have `content: \" \"; display: table`. Once `.contents` is `display:flex`, those pseudo-elements become flex items. They take part in ordering and `align-items`, and the `:after` item is placed before `.panel` (order 3). Floats on `.title` were removed, but the `.login-button`, `.icons` and `li` floats remain. This is probably harmless visually, but the clearfix is now dead weight and interacts with the `margin-left:auto` layout.",
